# Paths `lyrafmt` skips while walking a directory. One prefix per line, relative to the
# directory the walk began in; a name given on the command line is always formatted.
#
# The compiler's fixtures are inputs, not source: `syntax.lyra` is *meant* not to parse —
# it is what `lyrac check` is pointed at to produce a syntax error — so a formatter that
# walked into it would report it for ever and `lyrafmt --check .` could never be a CI step.
# The rest of the directory is here for the same reason: a fixture's text is the test, and
# the next one may be misformatted on purpose too.
cmd/lyrac/testdata/

# Generated by `bindings/imgui/gen/gen.lyra`, one wrapper to a line. Its test is that the
# generator reproduces it byte for byte (cmd/lyrac/imgui_example_test.go), so formatting it
# here would only make that test fail.
bindings/imgui/generated.lyra
